      "worked": "Write $y=2x^2+(2k+1)x-1$, so $a=2$, $b=2k+1$ and $c=-1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta &=(2k+1)^2-4(2)(-1)\\\\\\Delta &=(2k+1)^2+8>0\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $(2k+1)^2\\geq 0$, the discriminant is positive for every real $k$. Hence, the graph crosses the $x$-axis twice for every real $k$.",
